  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The paper presents conceptual frameworks and best practices rather than empirical data or case studies evaluating the real-world performance of these exercises.",
      "what": "This paper adapts established incident management practices into a series of company-neutral frameworks specifically tailored for automated vehicle (AV) emergency exercises. It details how to design, facilitate, and assess different exercise formats—including workshops, tabletop simulations, drills, and full-scale exercises—to address AV-specific socio-technical challenges ranging from collisions to natural hazards.",
      "why": "It provides the first structured guidance for AV incident response training, establishing a standardized methodology that allows different AV companies and public safety organizations to collaborate on emergency readiness."
    }
